# Repro: reserved SIMD intrinsic `iv_add` used as a variable name yields
# the misleading `expected identifier, got unknown` instead of a clear
# "reserved name" diagnostic.
#
#   cyrius test docs/development/issues/repros/2026-07-17-iv-intrinsic-var-name.cyr
#
# Actual:   error:<source>:1:5: expected identifier, got unknown
#               var iv_add = 1;
#                   ^
# Expected: either it compiles (intrinsics are contextual keywords, usable
#           as identifiers outside call position) OR a clear diagnostic:
#           "error: 'iv_add' is a reserved SIMD intrinsic; choose another name".
#
# iv_add / iv_sub / iv_mul (and iv_dp8) are the affected names.
# iv_div / iv_neg / iv_abs / iv_xyz are NOT intrinsics and compile fine —
# there is no integer-vector divide, which is exactly why iv_div is safe.
# Deterministic: 8/8. Reproduces on cycc 6.3.11, 6.4.5, 6.4.6, 6.4.65, 6.4.66.

include "lib/syscalls.cyr"

var iv_add = 1;
